Z||000000||OverDrive||05-29-2001||03:04 PM||||Hello! Im a new Fiero owner, I have an 84' Convertible. And I need to know 2 things.<BR>1) I have an automatic, is it really expensive to get it converted to a standard.<BR>and<BR>2) If I get a kit, how much time does it take to put together, and if its a lot of time, can I have someone else do it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||05-29-2001||03:15 PM||||if you have a convertible you already own a kit of sorts - would be a crime to use a fiero convertible as the donor chassis for a kit car.<P>  Pontaic did not make fiero convertibles - so yours has been retrofitted - very rare by the way.||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||05-29-2001||03:46 PM||||Welcome to the forum.  Since you want a standard trans and a kit car, it will be much easier to swap a car from me. hehe. It is probably a waste anyway to have a convertible in Canada.  Good luck with the car and you really have a rare one just the way it is.  Post some pics of the car. We love pics.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||p4n1c||05-29-2001||03:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>It is probably a waste anyway to have a convertible in Canada.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It doesn't snow year 'round here.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Actually the late spring and all summer, and most of the fall is usually pretty damn warm.  It's great for cruisin' with the top or windows down, or the sunroof out.<P>My uncle has a 4-4-2 convertible and it's wicked flying around the roads with the top down.  Your body is usually indented into the seat when he steps on it, but that's okay.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Feel lucky to own a rare Fiero, I wouldn't put a kit on it, I'd leave it as it is.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
